# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments
#
# .snakemake_envs/ holds the two conda envs the snakemake workflow builds via
# `make build-env` (see the root Snakefile). The others are historical: .venv and
# .simulation_running_venv are the pre-monorepo generation, .venv_modern and
# .test_venv were interim modern-suite environments from the migration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.conda_env/
.snakemake_envs/
.venv/
.simulation_running_venv/
.test_venv/
.venv_modern/

# FuzzyChecker per-run diagnostics. tests/reference/ is deliberately NOT ignored:
# it is the committed baseline the regression harness compares against.
tests/.diagnostics/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pipeline byproducts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.snakemake/
*.rdb
*.hdf
*.parquet
*.tmp
.cachedir
model_spec_int.yaml

# Simulation output, including the tens of gigabytes of duplicate psimulate worker
# logs, is already covered by the sub-gitignores: 0200_pregnancy_sim/.gitignore and
# 0300_child_sim/.gitignore both ignore `sim_results/`, and 0300 also ignores
# `lbwsg_pafs/`, `artifacts/` and `lbwsg_paf_artifacts/`. Deliberately not repeated
# here -- two places to update is how rules drift apart.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch, by convention dot-prefixed at the repo root
#
# Globs rather than one line per directory: this section had been growing an entry
# every time a run needed its output preserved, which is how it twice ended up
# corrupted by careless appends. Follow the convention and new scratch is covered
# automatically.
#
# Preserved pipeline output matters more than it sounds. The simulation rules
# `rm -rf` their results directory, and Snakemake deletes the outputs of a failed
# job, so anything not copied aside is unrecoverable -- the April-2025 parquet was
# lost exactly that way and exists nowhere. Preserve both sims, not just 0200.
#
# It is also deliberately NOT committed: the tracked CSVs are the 200-seed published
# GBD-2021 baseline that the whole regression harness compares against, and a rerun's
# output is neither that vintage nor that seed count.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.artifacts_*/
.sim_results_*/
.child_results_*/
.results_*/
.lbwsg_pafs_*/

# Local stand-in for the shared team model directory, via LSFF_MODEL_ROOT. Only
# created on branches carrying the paths.py override; harmless to ignore here.
.model_root*/

# Throwaway analysis scripts and run wrappers kept out of the way with a dot prefix.
.run_*.sh
.compare_*.py
.scratch_*
